WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Title: "Research your BOOT MENU KEY beforehand --
it's usually one of the ones below."

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.000
A laptop with a USB stick plugged in. Keys shown:
F2, F7, F9, F10, F11, F12, ESC, OPTION, NOVO.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.000
A hand presses the laptop's POWER button.
The screen turns on, blank and white.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.500
The hand taps the BOOT MENU KEY as the laptop
starts up. A spinning loading icon appears.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.500
A BOOT MENU opens, listing:
1. Hard Drive  2. CD-ROM  3. USB.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.500
Using the ARROW KEYS, the highlight moves down
the list: Hard Drive, then CD-ROM, then USB.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.000
"3. USB" is selected to boot from the USB stick.
The screen goes blank as it loads.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.600
"Kicksecure" appears with a green check mark
and a thumbs-up -- boot successful.
